        "username": "Arthur_Aihaken",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.eveonline.com/arthur_aihaken/{size}/504104_2.png",
        "created_at": "2025-02-01T09:07:13.019Z",
        "cooked": "<p>What defines “massive”? As <a class=\"mention\" href=\"/u/max_deveron\">@Max_Deveron</a> aptly pointed out, if we get to that point where we need AI players EVE is probably dead (or dying) anyway.</p>\n<p>Not that introducing more content in the form of AI players isn’t an intriguing idea, but if you introduce something like this don’t you open the floodgates to player bots?</p>\n<p>Side note: We do have NPC fleets that mine-out belts in high-sec. Sure there are a few other examples as well…</p>",
